0,Siouan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siouan-Catawban_languages,"January 1, 2026 - Siouan (/ˈsuːən/ SOO-ən), also known as Siouan–Catawban (/ˌsuːən kəˈtɔː.bən/ SOO-ən kə-TAW-bən), is a language family of North America located primarily in the Great Plains, Ohio and Mississippi valleys and southeastern North America with a few other languages in the east.",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
1,Sioux music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sioux_music,"September 3, 2025 - Sioux music prominently features the human voice, with songs accompanied by drumming. The Sioux are a large group of Native Americans generally divided into three subgroups: Lakota, Dakota and Nakota. They live on the northern prairies of North and South Dakota, Montana, Minnesota, and Nebraska, ...",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
2,Lakota Ceremonial Songs and Lyrics | PDF | Lakota | Siouan Peoples,https://www.scribd.com/document/294015804/Lakota-Ceremonial-Songs,"Lakota Ceremonial Songs - Free download as PDF File (.pdf), Text File (.txt) or read online for free. Traditional Lakota Ceremonial songs. Songs sacred to the Lakota People. Important heritage of the original people of North America",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
3,Lakota Yuwipi Ceremony Songs | PDF | Lakota | Siouan Peoples,https://www.scribd.com/document/437216900/Yuwipi-Songs-Lyrics-Complete-CD-pdf,"Yuwipi+Songs+Lyrics+Complete+CD.pdf - Free download as PDF File (.pdf), Text File (.txt) or read online for free. The document contains 10 Lakota ceremonial songs with their English translations. The songs are used in rituals like pipe filling, calling stones for a healing ceremony, prayers for wellness, and doctoring.",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
4,Sacred Songs of the Lakota - Prairie Edge.,https://prairieedge.com/tribe-scribe/sacred-songs-of-the-lakota/,"March 31, 2011 - But the mind cannot think, ""Great Spirit"" (Wakan Tanka) or conceive reality as it truly is. Thus, additional songs have been given to us - songs with music only - praise expressed throughout a few sacred syllables which go beyond the mind, beyond language and say the inexpressible, sing what is intellectually unutterable.",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
5,Lakota Music Project | South Dakota Symphony Orchestra,https://www.sdsymphony.org/education-community/lakota-music-project/,"The LMP concert program features combinations of South Dakota Symphony musicians, the Creekside Singers, a Lakota drumming group, and Dakota cedar flutist Bryan Akipa, each performing music of their heritages as well as unique repertoire ...",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
