9,Siouan-Catawban | Language Bibliography Wiki | Fandom,https://language-bibliography.fandom.com/wiki/Siouan-Catawban,"The Siouan-Catawban family includes the Siouan language family and the extinct Catawban language family, formerly spoken around South Carolina. The Siouan languages are spoken in the Plains and the Midwest, and formerly also in the Southeast and East. The term ""Siouan"" occasionally is used ...",Lakota,Siouan-Catawban
